	"description": [
		"Students learn, embody, and integrate elements of dance and film by engaging in the creative practice of making dance for the screen. Each student gaines experience as a director, performer, videographer, editor, and critic in this collaborative learning community. Students discuss and analyze live movement studies, screendances by peers and professionals, and relevant texts. Other technologies, such as 3D character animation and reactive/interactive technology, may be introduced. The class culminates with an evening public showing. Offered alternate years. Counts toward media and film studies concentrations."
	],
